        <object id="notif-mod-core" label="&lt;b&gt;core&lt;/b&gt; events (run_handler), jobs, ratelimit, runtime_config, db (advisory locks)" status="implemented" milestone="M0" source="backend/app/core/events.py; backend/app/core/jobs.py; backend/app/core/ratelimit.py; backend/app/core/runtime_config.py; backend/app/core/db.py"><mxCell style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=10;spacing=8;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1220" y="580" width="340" height="55" as="geometry" /></mxCell></object>
        <object id="notif-mod-outbox" label="&lt;b&gt;Outbox&lt;/b&gt; events of six modules in (dispatch_outbox every 5 s); nothing out" status="implemented" milestone="M0" source="backend/app/core/events.py"><mxCell style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=10;spacing=8;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1220" y="700" width="340" height="50" as="geometry" /></mxCell></object>
        <mxCell id="notif-mod-rule" value="&lt;b&gt;Rules&lt;/b&gt; (M6-DESIGN D104, D106, D112; test_architecture.py). Nobody imports notifications. It may import app.core, deeds.service and identity.service, and from feed, media, scoring and fraud only the named event classes and the three feed reads. Rows hold ids, codes and numbers only; text is rendered on read. Members never see fraud wording, case data or other subjects (D101). Email and push are M6B (not built)." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=12;align=left;spacingLeft=6;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="815" width="1140" height="70" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
